From: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: match each config symbol's #cmakedefine form to its use

#cmakedefine01 always emits a definition -- "#define X 0" for false -- so any
symbol declared that way is permanently `defined()`. Three symbols are tested
for existence rather than value, and each is therefore stuck on:

  * C_SYSTEM_ZLIB_NG, zmbv.h:  #if defined(C_SYSTEM_ZLIB_NG)
    Always true, so zmbv.h unconditionally pulls in <zlib-ng.h> and remaps
    deflate/inflate onto zng_*. Distributions that build zlib-ng in
    ZLIB_COMPAT mode -- where it is the zlib provider and installs only
    zlib.h -- fail to compile:
        zmbv.h:13:10: fatal error: zlib-ng.h: No such file or directory

  * C_UNALIGNED_MEMORY, vga_draw.cpp:  #if !defined(C_UNALIGNED_MEMORY)
    Always false, so the aligned-access fallback is never compiled -- even on
    arm64/aarch64, where CMakeLists.txt deliberately sets it OFF.

  * C_MANYMOUSE, mouse.cpp:  #ifndef C_MANYMOUSE
    Always false, so IsMappingSupported() reports Supported even in a build
    with OPT_MANYMOUSE=OFF.

The meson build is unaffected: #mesondefine leaves an unset key as
/* #undef */, which is what these tests expect.

Switch the first two to plain #cmakedefine, which gives meson's semantics.
C_MANYMOUSE cannot follow -- seven other sites use it as a value (#if
C_MANYMOUSE), which needs #cmakedefine01 -- so fix its one odd guard instead.

Signed-off-by: Carlos Martins <cjom@reglinux.org>
---
diff --git a/src/dosbox_config.h.in.cmake b/src/dosbox_config.h.in.cmake
index 62f1a3a..6d9c90f 100644
--- a/src/dosbox_config.h.in.cmake
+++ b/src/dosbox_config.h.in.cmake
@@ -42,7 +42,7 @@
 #cmakedefine01 C_TARGET_CPU_X86
 
 // Define to 1 if target CPU supports unaligned memory access
-#cmakedefine01 C_UNALIGNED_MEMORY
+#cmakedefine C_UNALIGNED_MEMORY
 
 // Define to 1 if the target platform needs per-page dynamic core write or execute (W^X) tagging
 #cmakedefine01 C_PER_PAGE_W_OR_X
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@
 // between operating systems.
 
 // Define to 1 when zlib-ng support is provided by the system
-#cmakedefine01 C_SYSTEM_ZLIB_NG
+#cmakedefine C_SYSTEM_ZLIB_NG
 
 // Defined if synchronous I/O multiplexing is available
 #cmakedefine HAVE_FD_ZERO
diff --git a/src/hardware/input/mouse.cpp b/src/hardware/input/mouse.cpp
index b0299bb..55e26d2 100644
--- a/src/hardware/input/mouse.cpp
+++ b/src/hardware/input/mouse.cpp
@@ -767,7 +767,7 @@ bool MouseControlAPI::IsMappingBlockedByDriver()
 
 MouseControlAPI::MappingSupport MouseControlAPI::IsMappingSupported()
 {
-#ifndef C_MANYMOUSE
+#if !C_MANYMOUSE
 	return MappingSupport::NotCompiledIn;
 #else
 #if defined(WIN32)
